<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear&nbsp;{!Contact.FirstName},</span></font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: arial;">Thank you for your interest in graduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU's diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. &nbsp;We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Applications for 2017 admission will be available on the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> in August. If you are interested in future study at ASU, please review the information below as guidelines for what to expect when you are ready to apply. For an idea of the course requirements for the various degree programs offered, select one of the checksheets accessible by your degree program interest <a href="https://music.asu.edu/degree-programs/graduate">here</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">Tuition and fees</a> at Arizona State University are reasonable, even for non-resident students. Music Scholarships and teaching assistantships are available. Typical assistantships are 25% which amount to 10 hours or work per week and receive:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">Tuition remission covering the non-resident portion of tuition</span></li><li><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">50% reduction in the resident portion of tuition (excluding fees)</span></li><li><span style="font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">$7,450 stipend for the academic year, distributed over bi-weekly paychecks</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Spoken English requirement</b>: If your native language is not English you must meet&nbsp;</span><a href="http://learnenglish.asu.edu/international-teaching-assistant" style="font-size: 12pt;">spoken English requirements</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> before you can be considered for a teaching assistantship. You may complete the ASU SPEAK test (minimum score of 55).Those wishing to be considered for Graduate Teaching Assistantships should submit a <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-teaching-assistants">TA application</a> by <b>February 15</b> for an appointment beginning fall semester.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>A few reminders for <a href="https://students.asu.edu/international/newgradstudents">prospective international graduate students</a></b>:</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ol><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">If you are from a country whose native language is not English, you must provide proof of English proficiency. Acceptable proof is as follows:&nbsp;</span></li></ol></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">TOEFL score of at least 550 (PBT) or 80 (iBT)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">IELTS overall band score of at least 6.5 with no band below 6.0</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Pearson Test of English (PTE) score of at least 60&nbsp;</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">It is <i>strongly</i> recommended to complete and pass the English proficiency exam prior to beginning the application process. Scores will be accepted for exams taken up to two years prior to your semester of admission.<b> Applications submitted without a passing TOEFL, IELTS, or PTE score will not be considered for admission</b>. For more information, please visit the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/proficiency">Graduate Education English proficiency website</a>. Another good resource for information on the international student application process is <a href="https://students.asu.edu/international">here</a>.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>2.&nbsp;</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">In addition to University <a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">tuition and fees</a>, international students <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>are required to enroll in the <a href="http://students.asu.edu/healthcoverageoptions">ASU student health insurance plan</a>. <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>More information about this requirement can be found <a href="http://students.asu.edu/internationalstudenthealth">here</a>.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>3.&nbsp;All transcripts and exam scores must be submitted directly to <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/apply">Graduate University Admissions office</a>. To process your <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>application, all <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/apply">international records</a> and official academic <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>credentials must be submitted in the original language <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>accompanied by an official English translation. Translations must <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>be literal, complete versions of the originals and must be <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>translated by a university, government official or official <span class="Apple-tab-span" style="white-space:pre">	</span>translation service. You cannot do your own translation.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Application Process</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 1</b>: You must first submit the Graduate Admissions application, followed by the School of Music application, before an audition or interview will be scheduled.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 2</b>: All transcripts and test scores must be submitted directly to the Graduate Admissions Office of the University.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 3</b>: Auditions or Interviews will be scheduled and application materials will be reviewed only after all application materials have been submitted. We are not responsible for application materials sent to the wrong office or directly to faculty. Please check the<a href="http://graduate.asu.edu/"> Graduate Education website</a> for application information, and the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> for specific application requirements for your degree program.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Applicants to the PhD Music Education, PhD Musicology, and DMA Composition programs</b> must submit GRE scores. The GRE examination in Music is not acceptable for admission to the doctoral program. GRE scores must be from within 5 years prior to the first day of the enrollment term.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Due to the high volume of applicants we receive each year, we recommend that you plan to apply as early as possible.</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees"><br></a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees">Rolling application deadlines</a>: Applications to the graduate program in music therapy and music education are accepted until all spaces are filled. Applicants are encouraged to apply as early as possible and prior to March for fall admission if they wish to be considered for scholarships. To ensure prompt processing of your application, please email <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a> after you have submitted your application.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">We welcome you to contact us via email to </span><a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu" style="font-size: 12pt;">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> if you have any additional questions. We also encourage you to refer to the School of Music Web site, </span><a href="https://music.asu.edu" style="font-size: 12pt;">music.asu.edu</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;">, as a resource for your admissions questions.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Best wishes,</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Office of Admissions</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">School of Music</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu"><font color="#ffcc66">music.asu.edu</font></a> | <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu"><font color="#ffcc66">musicadmissions@asu.edu</font></a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial" color="#ffffff">{!Case.Thread_Id}</font></div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>